## The two headline numbers

**The gain from reallocating the same budget:** {{ v('budget.headline.gain_over_last_year_annual') }} a
year over last year's mix, {{ v('budget.headline.gain_over_last_year_weekly') }} a week, judged on the
true curves. **The share of the truth optimal gain captured:** {{ v('budget.headline.share_captured') }}
for the calibrated plan and {{ v('budget.headline.share_captured_uncalibrated') }} for the uncalibrated
one, against the truth optimal plan's {{ v('budget.headline.gain_optimal_annual') }} a year. Both come
from one simulated market. The regret study below is the number to quote.

## The regret study

For each of {{ v('budget.regret.calibrated.seeds') }} seeds of the demonstration condition the market is
simulated, the geo test is run on it, own is fit before and after calibration, each fit's plan is
optimized under the same constraints, and every plan is judged on that market's true curves. The
calibrated plan captured {{ v('budget.regret.calibrated.share_captured') }} of the truth optimal gain
({{ v('budget.regret.calibrated.share_captured_lower') }} to {{ v('budget.regret.calibrated.share_captured_upper') }},
a bootstrap interval over seeds) and the uncalibrated plan {{ v('budget.regret.uncalibrated.share_captured') }}
({{ v('budget.regret.uncalibrated.share_captured_lower') }} to {{ v('budget.regret.uncalibrated.share_captured_upper') }}).
